Subject: DXVK dxso: compare depth textures in the shader, one image per binding
Date: 2026-10-24
Applies to: sources/dxvk (DXVK 1.10.3 cxaddon), after 0001
Files changed: src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp, src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp

For each sampler, DXVK's Direct3D 9 shader compiler declares a colour image
and a depth-compare ("shadow") image at the same binding and picks one with
a spec constant. MoltenVK 1.4.2 cannot translate that: with Metal argument
buffers SPIRV-Cross drops the shadow variant's sampler ("use of undeclared
identifier 's0_2d_shadowSmplr'"), and without them Metal rejects two
textures at one index ("cannot reserve 'texture' resource location"). In
Black Ops the screen stayed black: 42 and then 172 pixel shaders failed.

The depth-compare variant is no longer declared. When the spec constant
marks a sampler as a depth texture, the shader samples the colour image and
compares itself: 1.0 where the reference is <= the stored depth, else 0.0,
in every component, with the reference divided like the coordinates for a
projected sample (SM1's projected and unprojected samples are compared
separately before the existing select). Samplers of depth textures no longer
enable comparison. INTZ/DF16/DF24 reads are unchanged (they are not depth
textures for DXVK).

Review fixes (2026-10-24): the first version only dropped the variant, so
shadow maps returned the depth value instead of a comparison on every
driver, and a comparison sampler sampled a colour image (undefined in
Vulkan). Black Ops had to be played with shadows off (sm_enable 0); with
the comparison in the shader they can be turned on again.
Limit: one comparison per sample (no 2x2 PCF filtering of the results).
Test: tests/src/d3d9-shadow-test.c.
License: zlib, like the DXVK files it modifies.
